  "title": "RTPS: Fix OOB write in DATA_BATCH sample info list",
  "description": "dissect_RTPS_DATA_BATCH() allocates sample_info_flags[] and\nsample_info_length[] with sample_info_max entries, then fills them in the\nsample-info loop indexed by sample_info_count. The loop's bounds check\nonly fired when the max_batch_samples_dissected preference was > 0:\n\n  if (rtps_max_batch_samples_dissected > 0 && ... >= rtps_max_batch_samples_dissected)\n\nWhen the preference is set to 0 (a valid value meaning \"show up to 1024\"),\nsample_info_max is set to 1024 for the allocation, but the guard is\ndisabled entirely. A crafted DATA_BATCH submessage with many minimal\nsample-info records (~8 bytes each) then drives sample_info_count past\n1024, writing sample_info_flags[] and sample_info_length[] out of bounds\nin packet-scope (wmem) memory, and the stale entries are read again when\nthe batched samples are dissected.\n\nGuard on sample_info_max instead, which equals the preference when it is\n> 0 and 1024 when it is 0, so the loop can never exceed the allocation in\neither case.\n\nThis requires the non-default preference value of 0; with the default\n(16) the OOB write is not reachable.\n\nReported by Aisle Research.\n\nFixes #21508",
